    "title": "Chicago man caught on video pouring liquid on kids, parents leaving NW Side dance class charged - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By ABC7 Chicago Digital Team ,\n4 hours ago\nA 50-year-old Chicago man accused of throwing a liquid on a group of parents and children, who were making their way out of a Mexican folkloric dance class, has been charged, Chicago police said Wednesday.\nRobert Villanueva has been charged with battery in the incident.\nABC7 Chicago is now streaming 24/7. Click here to watch Video of the incident has gone viral. It happened about 10 p.m. Friday night near Belmont Avenue and Pulaski Road on Chicago's Northwest Side.\nA woman's heard saying to dancers with the Ballet Folklorico de Chicago, \"you're lucky ICE isn't here.\"\nThen, the man throws the liquid.\nThe Belmont Gardens dance studio, parents and children said they feel like they're under attack.\nThe couple involved spoke with ABC7 Chicago and admitted their actions were wrong.\nThey said they feel threatened by the backlash they have received.\nVillanueva is due in court April 9.",
    "summary": "By ABC7 Chicago Digital Team , A 50-year-old Chicago man accused of throwing a liquid on a group of parents and children, who were making their way out of a Mexican folkloric dance class, has been charged, Chicago police said Wednesday. It happened about 10 p.m. Friday night near Belmont Avenue and Pulaski Road on Chicago's Northwest Side. A woman's heard saying to dancers with the Ballet Folklorico de Chicago, \"you're lucky ICE isn't here.\" The Belmont Gardens dance studio, parents and children said they feel like they're under attack.",
